<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107180" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπεπιμόριος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		an arithmetical term, the reciprocal of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιμόριος,</span> represented by the fraction <i><span class="en">
			1
		</span></i>/(<i><span class="en">
			1
		</span></i> + <i><span class="en">
			1
		</span></i>/n) or n/(n + <i><span class="en">
			1
		</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
			Arist.
			<u>Metaph.</u>
			1021a2
		</span></i>:—so <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφημιόλιος</span></b>  is the reciprocal of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμιόλιος</span> (<i><span class="en">
			2
		</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
			3
		</span></i> of <i><span class="en">
			3
		</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
			2
		</span></i>), <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπεπίτριτος</span></b>  of
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίτριτος</span> (<i><span class="en">
			3
		</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
			4
		</span></i> of <i><span class="en">
			4
		</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
			3
		</span></i>), <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπεπιτέταρτος</span></b>  of
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτέταρτος</span> (<i><span class="en">
			4
		</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
			5
		</span></i> of <i><span class="en">
			5
		</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
			4
		</span></i>), <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπεπόγδοος</span></b>  of
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπόγδοος</span> (<i><span class="en">
			8
		</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
			9
		</span></i> of <i><span class="en">
			9
		</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
			8
		</span></i>), etc., <i><span class="en">
			Nicom.
			<u>Ar.</u>
			1.19
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>Exc.</u>
			2
		</span></i>, Theo Sm.<i><span class="en">
			p.75
		</span></i> H., etc.; and so <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπεπιμερής</span></b>  is the reciprocal of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιμερής,</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Nicom.
			<u>Ar.</u>
		</span></i>l.c.—These ratios are called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόλογοι, ἐπιμόριος</span> etc. being <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόλογοι.</span></div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>